Rule 2 (all shape dimensions are non-negative; empty shapes allowed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (scalar input must still use a supported dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10)
>>
Rule 4 (boolean and integer/uint dtypes are not allowed for isnan)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 2 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 3 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 4 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 5
>>
Rule 5 (unsupported dtypes are rejected via guard)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) then true else false
